hadowing alarm go off when marcus  says this about sue becoming a believer  maybe she might come around paul's mouse  one he received from trust as a reward  for telling him the whereabouts of the  believers was actually implanted with a  bile bomb a sneaky attempt by trust to  kill the believers without sacrificing  their own men this ends up causing a  violent contagion that covers paul in  some sort of cocoon but before he slips  into unconsciousness we see his pupils  turn into slits almost serpent-like we  do know that trust has been collecting  samples from the serpents so perhaps  they're using these samples to create  new and deadly bio weapons it also seems  that marcus is unaffected by this virus  likely due to mother's eyes which will  later get removed from his stomach  marcus prays to saul to help save his  son while also chastising vril for being  the one to bring the boys to their  campsite in the first place if ril had  never done that paul in all likelihood  would be fine this is all part of a  gradual build-up to pit vril against her  own mother decima campion rushes off to  get help from mother believing her to be  the only hope for paul's survival but  this would put the believers in jeopardy  so decima orders her robot daughter to  stop him it's a move that forces real to  attack campion but because she can't  stray from a direct order she has to do  it a bit of a budding romance has  sprouted between these two which makes  the scene all the more compelling back  at atheist camp father hunter and  tempest relish in their victory over the  industrial droid billy last episode this  one father a can of fuel blood which he  believes will help revive the million  year old android he's been putting  together for the last few episodes  tempest also tells them the guy she hung  out with at the scrap market belongs to  a different encampment one she promised  to give up her baby to you may recall  that tempus child was the result of her  being raped by mithra clerk named otho  father shows hunter and tempest what  he's been working on and relates its  creation more akin to farming than  engineering at first it doesn't seem to  react to the fuel blood but as father  and the others leave it sucks that  liquid right up mother rips apart poor  vita's necromancer game which is what  gives her the idea to use one of its  microchips to control the serpent we see  her testing it on a bird but it doesn't  go over too well sue also questions  mother about the origin of the serpent  knowing that mother is actually its mom  last episode she learned that mother's  pregnancy and the birth of the serpent  line up perfectly in arguably one of the  most wtf moments of the episode campion  is attacked by real only for her to be  attacked by this weird-looking creature  a creature which has evolved to  withstand the acidic waters we've seen  other such creatures on kepler back in  season one so it seems as though there  are different types of species that have  adapted to the planet's various  ecosystems that being said i don't think  one of these creatures has enough  strength to completely pull a giant  container into the ocean on its own so  who knows what else lurks beneath the  acidic water rill's injury does not  allow her to chase after campion like  her direct order stated but something  the show has been hinting at is a  robot's ability to override its core  directives and make their own decisions  when mother confronts trust he says that  it's impossible for him to promise  protection to her children because it's  against his core programming to not  treat everyone equally there are some  out there who believe that trust is  actually saul before he's learned to  override its programming the evidence on  this is pretty thin but it's definitely  possible and as i stated in my episode 1  and 2 breakdown one of the ancient tarot  cards does look strikingly similar to  truss core tamerlane chases after  campion but the two are o